CamelMailer began as a ground-up Rust rewrite of Postal. Portions of its
design, its data model, its configuration format and its wire behaviour
derive from that project, and its Postal compatibility surface (the
`postal:` config group alias, `POSTAL_CONFIG_FILE_PATH`, the
`X-Postal-MsgID` header and the webhook payload shapes) exists so a Postal
installation can move across without changing its integrations.

